nstructionsStep 1: Extract the Palm Nut Juice (If using fresh nuts)Wash 500 g – 1 kg of fresh palm nuts and boil them in water until tender (about 20–30 minutes).   Drain, transfer to a mortar, and pound gently to separate the pulp from the hard seeds.   Place the pounded pulp in a bowl, add warm water, and knead with your hands to release the rich juice.   Strain through a fine mesh sieve to remove all fibers and seeds. Set the thick liquid aside.Step 2: Prepare the Vegetables & CornCorn: Wash the fresh corn cobs and slice the kernels off the cob using a knife.   Greens: Pluck the Zom leaves from the stems, wash them thoroughly in clean water, and chop or shred them finely.   Step 3: Cook the Corn & GreensIn a large pot, add the fresh corn kernels with about 2 cups of water.   Cover and boil over medium-high heat for about 15–20 minutes until the corn begins to soften and the water reduces significantly.   Layer the shredded greens directly on top of the cooking corn.   Stir gently and allow the greens to wilt and cook in the remaining steam until almost all the excess water in the pot has dried up. (Crucial tip: Let the cooking water dry first so it doesn't dilute the palm cream later).   Step 4: Add the Palm Nut Juice & SimmerPour the extracted palm nut juice (or canned pulp mixed with a little water) directly into the pot with the corn and greens.   Add a whole hot pepper if you like a touch of heat.Lower the heat to medium-low and let the mixture simmer for 20–30 minutes.   Stir frequently: Stir regular, sweeping movements across the bottom of the pot to prevent the thick palm juice from scorching.   Cook until the dish thickens to a porridge-like consistency and the palm oil begins to gloss on top.Step 5: Season & ServeTaste the Sanga. If you prefer a sweet dish, stir in sugar to your liking at the very end.   Remove from heat and serve hot.Serving Suggestions
